      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal|Guarded Write Journal]] page describes a mechanism used by the guarded write path to ensure reliable, all-or-nothing writes:\n\n**Key points:**\n\n- **Prior state recording**: Before overwriting any file, the system journals (records) the file\u0027s previous state \u2014 either its prior content if it existed, or a record that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n- **In-memory transaction log**: The journal is held in memory for the duration of a single agent run, serving as a transaction log without requiring a database.\n\n- **Rollback on failure**: If an agent run fails (e.g., due to exceeding turn caps or unrecoverable errors), the journal rolls back every recorded write in reverse order \u2014 restoring previous file content or deleting newly created files.\n\n- **All-or-nothing semantics**: This gives each run all-or-nothing semantics for its writes, meaning either all writes succeed or all are rolled back.\n\n- **Limited scope**: The Query agent doesn\u0027t use the rollback path since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library for agents that do write.",
